-- title:
--   An anchored word bound with an early-head reserve
-- statement:
--   Write $I_n=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, with cyclic arithmetic modulo $n$ and integer representatives for inequalities; $[x]_n$ denotes the least nonnegative residue when $n>0$. For a permutation $p$ and anchor $a$, let $q_a(i)=p(i)+a-p(a)$, $h_a=|\{i:q_a(i)<i\}|$, $D^a_i=((q_a(i)-i)\bmod n)-h_a$, and $c_a=a-p(a)-h_a$. Words use a forward cyclic rotation $L$ and the exchange $X=(0\ 1)$; $\operatorname{ev}(w)$ is their permutation product and $|w|$ their number of letters. Let $n\ge2$ and $h_a>0$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \exists v:\ p\operatorname{ev}(v)=1,\quad |v|\le h_a(n-h_a-1)+(h_a+2)(n-1)-h_a.
--   $$
--
--   The early nonmaximal head improves the uniform anchored sorting estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/HeadReserve.lean#L110-L174

